+## Clean-clone setup
+
+Run every command in this guide from the ExecuTorch repository root. Use the
+checkout's installer rather than installing an unrelated `executorch` wheel
+from PyPI:
+
+```bash
+python3.12 -m venv .venv
+source .venv/bin/activate
+
+./install_executorch.sh --optional-dependency ethos_u
+
+./examples/arm/setup.sh --i-agree-to-the-contained-eula
+source examples/arm/arm-scratch/setup_path.sh
+```
+
+`install_executorch.sh` installs the current checkout and Ethos-U Python tools
+into the active virtual environment. `examples/arm/setup.sh` installs the
+pinned Arm GNU bare-metal toolchain and Corstone FVP used by this example.
+For a later editable reinstall, the equivalent package command is
+`python -m pip install -e '.[ethos_u]' --no-build-isolation`. There is no
+`cortex_m` package extra; CMSIS-NN kernels are selected when building a target
+runtime, and this example does not need them because its graph is fully
+delegated to Ethos-U.
+
+On macOS, install the
+[FVPs-on-Mac](https://github.com/Arm-Examples/FVPs-on-Mac) Docker wrapper and
+add its `bin` directory to `PATH` before running the setup or smoke commands.
+Run `command -v FVP_Corstone_SSE-320` and confirm it resolves inside the
+FVPs-on-Mac `bin` directory rather than to a downloaded Linux FVP binary.
+
+## One-command end-to-end smoke test
+
+After setup, export, build, run on Corstone-320 FVP, and validate the target
+mask with:
+
+```bash
+./backends/arm/test/test_arm_ootb.sh run_mobilesam_e2e_ethos_u
+```
