diff --git a/zephyr/samples/mobilesam-ethosu/README.md b/zephyr/samples/mobilesam-ethosu/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..2ee8292290
--- /dev/null
+++ b/zephyr/samples/mobilesam-ethosu/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,194 @@
+# Live MobileSAM on Alif Ensemble E8
+
+This Zephyr sample captures the Alif E8 Development Kit's on-board MT9M114
+selfie camera, runs MobileSAM on the Cortex-M55 HP core and Ethos-U85-256, and
+draws up to four distinct masks on the 480x800 display. The dashboard includes
+the ExecuTorch and PyTorch logos, inference time, and detected-object count.
+
+The model is stored separately in external OSPI flash at `0xC0000000`. Point
+prompts are fixed during export; the recommended four-point grid samples each
+image quadrant and target-side post-processing removes duplicate masks.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Alif Ensemble E8 Development Kit with its display and selfie camera attached.
+- Alif's `zephyr_alif` and `sdk-alif` checkouts. These revisions are tested:
+  - `zephyr_alif`: `f002a4d8499c35fc70ec4d5324faa7b01c152c72`
+  - `sdk-alif`: `1db82c9d0cc594e2b548a13699e8a4157e6dcd4c`
+- Zephyr SDK 0.17.0 and a Python environment containing `west`, `fdt`, and the
+  Alif Zephyr requirements.
+- ExecuTorch's Arm dependencies from `examples/arm/setup.sh`.
+- Alif Security Toolkit and SEGGER J-Link software.
+
+Use the [Arm Alif E8 board setup guide](https://learn.arm.com/learning-paths/embedded-and-microcontrollers/alif-image-classification/board-setup/)
+for a new board. Leave SW4 in its default SEUART position. Close terminal
+programs connected to the SEUART port before using SETOOLS; no further SW4
+changes are required by this workflow.
+
+The commands below assume:
+
+```bash
+export EXECUTORCH_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/executorch
+export ZEPHYR_BASE=/absolute/path/to/zephyr_alif
+export SDK_ALIF=/absolute/path/to/sdk-alif
+export ZEPHYR_SDK_INSTALL_DIR=/absolute/path/to/zephyr-sdk-0.17.0
+export ZEPHYR_TOOLCHAIN_VARIANT=zephyr
+export MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT=/absolute/path/to/mobilesam-alif-e8
+export MOBILE_SAM_SOURCE="$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/mobile-sam/source"
+
+mkdir -p "$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT"
+cd "$EXECUTORCH_ROOT"
+```
+
+Initialize the west workspace and Python dependencies once:
+
+```bash
+west init -l "$ZEPHYR_BASE"
+west update
+python -m pip install -r "$ZEPHYR_BASE/scripts/requirements.txt"
+python -m pip install fdt west
+west zephyr-export
+```
+
+Keep this ExecuTorch Python environment active for export and build. CMake uses
+its interpreter to inspect the PTE and generate model-specific sources.
+
+## Export the live multi-object model
+
+Prepare the pinned MobileSAM checkout, then export a 384x384 quantized-I/O
+model with four independent point prompts and three candidates per point:
+
+```bash
+python examples/arm/mobilesam_prompt_segmentation_example_ethos_u/model_export/prepare_mobilesam.py \
+  --source-dir "$MOBILE_SAM_SOURCE"
+
+python examples/arm/mobilesam_prompt_segmentation_example_ethos_u/model_export/export_mobilesam.py \
+  --output-path "$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/mobilesam_live_384_grid4_multimask.pte" \
+  --mobile-sam-source "$MOBILE_SAM_SOURCE" \
+  --image examples/models/dinov2/dog.jpg \
+  --input-size 384 \
+  --point 96 96 \
+  --point 288 96 \
+  --point 96 288 \
+  --point 288 288 \
+  --multimask-output \
+  --quantized-io
+```
+
+The export also writes
+`mobilesam_live_384_grid4_multimask.json`. The sample rejects models that have
+CPU operators, non-int8 I/O, or an incompatible output layout.
+
+Copy the PTE byte-for-byte for J-Link:
+
+```bash
+cp "$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/mobilesam_live_384_grid4_multimask.pte" \
+  "$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/mobilesam_live_384_grid4_multimask.bin"
+cmp "$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/mobilesam_live_384_grid4_multimask.pte" \
+  "$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/mobilesam_live_384_grid4_multimask.bin"
+```
+
+## Build
+
+`SDK_ALIF` lets CMake select sdk-alif's official MT9M114 selfie-camera overlay.
+The application adds the deferred sensor initialization needed by its explicit
+power-up sequence.
+
+```bash
+west build \
+  -d "$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/build-mobilesam-live" \
+  -p always \
+  -b alif_e8_dk/ae822fa0e5597xx0/rtss_hp \
+  "$EXECUTORCH_ROOT/zephyr/samples/mobilesam-ethosu" -- \
+  -DZEPHYR_EXTRA_MODULES="$EXECUTORCH_ROOT;$SDK_ALIF" \
+  -DSDK_ALIF="$SDK_ALIF" \
+  -DET_PTE_FILE_PATH="$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/mobilesam_live_384_grid4_multimask.pte" \
+  -DMODEL_METADATA_PATH="$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/mobilesam_live_384_grid4_multimask.json" \
+  -DPython3_EXECUTABLE="$(command -v python)"
+```
+
+A tested build used 7,580,784 bytes of the 7,602,176-byte application RAM
+region and 768,064 bytes of the 786,432-byte SRAM0 region. The application
+checks the PTE's required Ethos-U scratch size during configuration.
+
+## Flash a new board
+
+First complete the one-time SETOOLS board setup from the Arm guide. Keep SW4 in
+SEUART, disconnect any serial terminal, and set the Security Toolkit path:
+
+```bash
+export ALIF_SE_TOOLS_DIR=/absolute/path/to/alif-security-toolkit
+export ALIF_DEVICE=AE822FA0E5597_HP
+export JLINK_COMMANDER=/absolute/path/to/JLinkExe
+```
+
+Flash a small idle application before changing OSPI contents. This prevents a
+running XIP application from holding the flash controller:
+
+```bash
+west build \
+  -d "$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/build-ospi-idle" \
+  -p always \
+  -b alif_e8_dk/ae822fa0e5597xx0/rtss_hp \
+  "$ZEPHYR_BASE/samples/hello_world" -- \
+  -DZEPHYR_EXTRA_MODULES="$SDK_ALIF"
+
+west flash -d "$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/build-ospi-idle" \
+  --runner alif_flash -- --device "$ALIF_DEVICE"
+```
+
+Power-cycle the board, then start J-Link Commander:
+
+```bash
+"$JLINK_COMMANDER" \
+  -device AE822FA0E5597LS0_M55_HP \
+  -if SWD \
+  -speed 4000 \
+  -autoconnect 1
+```
+
+At the J-Link prompt, program and verify the model while the target is halted:
+
+```text
+halt
+loadbin /absolute/path/to/mobilesam_live_384_grid4_multimask.bin,0xC0000000
+verifybin /absolute/path/to/mobilesam_live_384_grid4_multimask.bin,0xC0000000
+exit
+```
+
+Flash the final firmware through SETOOLS and power-cycle once more:
+
+```bash
+west flash -d "$MOBILE_SAM_OUTPUT/build-mobilesam-live" \
+  --runner alif_flash -- --device "$ALIF_DEVICE"
+```
+
+The PTE only needs to be programmed again after re-exporting the model. Normal
+firmware rebuilds require only the final `west flash` command.
+
+## Expected result
+
+After the sensor's initial stabilization interval, the display continuously
+updates with the live camera image and colored segmentation overlays. A tested
+E8 processed a frame in about 1.34 seconds and selected two distinct objects in
+a representative scene. The exact mask count and timing depend on the scene.
+
+When a console is available, each completed frame also prints:
+
+```text
+Frame 9: 1340 ms, 2 objects
+```
+
+## Limitations
+
+- This sample targets the Alif E8 DK hardware and its bundled MT9M114 camera;
+  other boards need their own camera, display, memory, and power configuration.
+- The four prompt coordinates are compiled into the PTE. Re-export to change
+  the grid or input resolution.
+- Up to four distinct masks are displayed. The model emits three candidates
+  per point; the application filters low-quality, oversized, and duplicate
+  masks.
+- Camera capture and display share the board's external MIPI route, so the
+  application alternates them after each frame.
+- The PTE is not linked into the firmware and must remain at OSPI address
+  `0xC0000000`.
